Because of the downsides. The dungeon levels up with the character. The
protection price also levels up with the character. You've admitted both
in your list above.

So a temporary suspension of levelling up to get the free AC is a smart bet.
And as you point out since minimal levelling up isn't too damaging, you can
balance the MPR by levelling up to XL2 (or maybe even XL3), not tipping the
dungeon too badly and finishing the MPR run.

It isn't permanent. It's minimal cost. You get great AC and a really good
pet out of it. You'll level up really quickly as soon as you're finished.
It teaches defensive nethacking skills, which is probably what folks who
have never ascended need. It unbalances the game in your favor, which rarely
rarely happens.

Levelling up isn't free. Truthfully neither is the AC. But properly managed
it can be low cost and serve you in multiple capacities for the rest of the 
game (lower AC/weight ration, lower hit percentage, lower damage/hit).

